---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="Kilnbook for schools and colleges"
	description="Wheel booking, kiln firing queues and class rosters for school and college ceramics departments with one or two kilns and a semester timetable."
>
	<section class="band-dark page-hero">
		<div class="wrap">
			<p class="eyebrow">For schools &amp; colleges</p>
			<h1>A ceramics room that runs between the bells.</h1>
			<p class="lede narrow">
				One or two kilns, a semester of sections, and students who want a wheel in the free hour
				before their next class. Kilnbook keeps the wheels, the kiln shelves and the class lists in
				one place, so the studio tech is not refereeing a sign-up sheet.
			</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn">Book a demo</a>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Wheel time between classes</h2>
		<p>
			Students reserve wheels, hand-building tables and the slab roller in one-hour blocks, so a free period turns into throwing time instead of a hunt for an open wheel. You decide
			how many hours each membership tier gets each week and how far ahead they can book, and freed-up slots
			appear on the calendar as soon as someone cancels.
			<a href="/features/wheel-time">How wheel booking works</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>One queue per kiln</h2>
		<p>
			Students log a piece when they set it on the bisque shelf. Each kiln has its own queue for
			bisque and glaze firings, you can see how full each load is, and every student with work in a
			load gets a text when it is unloaded. The firing log records the date, cone, schedule and who
			loaded it. <a href="/features/firings">How firing queues work</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Sections that follow the semester</h2>
		<p>
			Set up each course as a fixed series that runs for the length of your term, and add drop-in
			open studio sessions alongside it. Instructors get their own login with the roster for the day,
			can mark attendance from the studio tablet and leave notes for the next instructor.
			<a href="/features/classes">How classes work</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Which plan fits a department</h2>
		<p>
			The Studio plan covers up to 3 kilns with unlimited members, which suits most departments with
			one or two kilns and a full roster of students. If you run studios on more than one campus,
			Collective has no kiln limit and one account across locations.
			<a href="/pricing">Compare plans</a>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Questions departments ask</h2>
		<div class="faq">
			<details>
				<summary>We have two kilns. Which plan do we need?</summary>
				<p>
					The Studio plan covers up to 3 kilns and unlimited members, so two kilns and every student
					in your program fit on one plan. If you add a fourth kiln later, you can move to Collective
					at any point in the month.
				</p>
			</details>
			<details>
				<summary>Is there pricing for schools?</summary>
				<p>
					Yes. School ceramics programs and registered nonprofits get 30% off any plan. Mention it
					when you book a demo.
				</p>
			</details>
			<details>
				<summary>Can we import our students from a class list?</summary>
				<p>
					Yes. Upload a CSV with names and emails, and we map the columns for you during setup.
				</p>
			</details>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="cta-band">
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2>See it in your ceramics room</h2>
			<p>30 days free on the Studio plan. No card to start.</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn btn-dark">Book a demo</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
